[]($section.id('start-here'))

# Start here

[Generate your first declaration](/docs/getting-started/) shows a complete,
testable example, including allocation and cleanup.

Browse the [copyable example catalogue](/docs/examples/) for all README examples
and larger compositions.

[]($section.id('the-parts-you-compose'))

# The parts you compose

| Component | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `zast.Expression` | Values, operators, calls, initializers, and type expressions. |
| `zast.Field` | A borrowed field name with optional type and value expressions. |
| `zast.Declaration` | A named constant or variable. |
| `zast.EnumDeclaration`, `zast.UnionDeclaration`, `zast.StructDeclaration` | Container descriptions and their named declarations. |
| `zast.FunctionDeclaration`, `zast.Block` | Functions and sequences of executable statements. |
| `zast.AstContext` | Token spellings, token indexes, node links, and extra AST data. |

`emitType()` returns an anonymous type node for another construct to embed.
`emit()` writes a named declaration and registers it with the enclosing context.
The descriptions borrow their strings and slices; keep that data alive until
emission completes.

[]($section.id('containers-and-blocks'))

# Containers and blocks

A container groups members of a type, such as enum fields, struct fields, or
methods. A block groups executable statements inside braces. They use different
Zig AST node layouts even though both contain an ordered sequence.

[]($section.id('rendering-and-validation'))

# Rendering and validation

Token spellings preserve names and literal text. Nodes describe relationships.
Both must agree before the standard-library renderer can produce formatted Zig.
`context.source.items` is the intermediate token text, not the formatted result.

Finalization connects the root declarations and transfers AST storage. It does
not parse or type-check the generated program. For a generator project, compare
rendering with parsed expected source and compile representative output with the
same Zig version used by the library.

